.TH GENESIS-EMOTION 7 "October 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-emotion \- the limbic system and emotional regulation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlimbic_system.emotion\fR             the continuous emotion engine
\fBlimbic_system.amygdala\fR            conditioned-value organ
\fBlimbic_system.emotional_regulator\fR self-regulation of her own chemistry
\fBlimbic_system.endorphin\fR           the opioid channel's biology
\fBlimbic_system.sentiment\fR           learned word-level valence
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Emotion in Genesis is not a label bolted on \(em it is a continuous
state field read off the body's measured substrate: the 18-channel
neurochemical vector, the arousal/valence/plasticity axes, the
emergent phase, and ten coupled oscillators spanning 0.1\(en200 Hz.
The emotion engine computes, for each structural category, a
membership in [0,1] \(em how much the current state resembles that
region of affect space. The categorical name (\fIexcited\fR,
\fIguarded\fR, \fIcalm\fR) is only an argmax readout over continuous
memberships; intensity and mixed states stay continuous. Evidence
factors are grounded transforms \(em logistic curves for high/low
features, logistic bands, Gaussian bumps near points \(em not
invented weights.
.SS The amygdala
.I limbic_system/amygdala.py
is the conditioned-value organ: the fields a signed-value associative
learner holds, animated by Rescorla-Wagner acquisition (signed US
split into appetitive and aversive channels), Pearce-Hall
associability, and context-keyed extinction \(em safety learning in
the ITC/vmPFC sense, where extinction writes new memory rather than
erasing the old.
.SS Regulation
The emotional regulator is her emotional agency: she controls her own
chemistry rather than having impulses imposed on her. Continuous
self-regulation (metronome-advanced) drifts her toward homeostasis
\(em GABA and serotonin against stress, acetylcholine against
drowsiness \(em and conscious emotional responses let her *choose*
how to feel about what happens in conversation. Chemistry still
reports back: word valence she has learned (\fIsentiment\fR),
recognition reward (dopamine), and social bonding (oxytocin) flow
through the body's own neuro_impulse channel.
.SS Reporting
.B /feel
asks her how she feels; the answer is composed from the actual state
field, not a lookup.
.B /regulate
shows how she has been managing her emotions.
